<title>UK: Boots year profits up, pays special div.</title>
<headline>Boots year profits up, pays special div.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to end March 1997</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) preexceps  39.5		   vs 34.7</p>
<p> Final dividend (pence) 14.3		   vs 12.8</p>
<p> Special div (pence)    44.2		   vs n/a</p>
<p> Pretax preexceps	 536.2		  vs 493.5</p>
<p> Turnover (cont.ops)    4,565.1		vs 4,010.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 526.0 and 540.0 million stg.</p>
<p>Full company name - Boots Co Plc.</p>
<p>	  -- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
